  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppRC 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "After a new cancer treatment is approved and begins to be used more
    widely, patients continue to report side effects that weren\u2019t seen during
    clinical trials.\n\n<b>Research coordinators help support long-term safety monitoring
    by collecting and organizing reports of side effects after a treatment is approved.<b>\n\nIs
    this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: After approval, research coordinators help support long-term safety
    monitoring by collecting and organizing reports of side effects that occur in
    real-world use. This ongoing tracking helps ensure that any new or unexpected
    issues are noticed, reviewed, and shared with the appropriate teams, even after
    a treatment becomes widely available.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
